it(W2, "ExecRegressionC1", "executor", """Final no-harm run for C1 on quiescent bytes (poll until {WD}/ExecCounterFix.md exists, then run): from {LANE}: `python3 corpus/instruments/limb-mutation-check.py --ledger corpus/instruments/limb-ledger.json` (twice, byte-identical), `python3 corpus/instruments/limb-mutation-check.py --selftest`, `python3 corpus/instruments/recheck-audit.py --quiet` (expect strict pass=44/44 exit 0 after the F15 entry), `python3 corpus/instruments/recheck-audit.py --selftest`, `python3 corpus/instruments/source-recheck.py --selftest`, `python3 corpus/instruments/anchorcheck.py --selftest`, `python3 corpus/instruments/frontier-recheck-count.py` (entries=18 pass=18 exit=0), every registered source-recheck on manifests rounds 23-31 (`--source` each id), `python3 corpus/instruments/score-gap.py --selftest`; each from lane root AND `cd / &&` with `--root`/absolute paths where the tool supports it. Label every value; write {WD}/ExecRegressionC1.md with outputs and sha256 of all instruments + ledger. Report any non-zero exit with the owning seat.""")
it(W2, "CritCalibration", "critic", """Calibration attack (AXES calibration: self-assessment vs observed state). Read SHONEN.md, SCORECARD.md (round-30 section, Axes, Capabilities, Saturation), corpus/README.md coverage statements, corpus/instruments/README.md, and the landed round-31 bytes. Count mismatches between the lane's self-assessment and observed state with commands: stale numbers (`grep -n` for registry row counts, frontier counts, `entries=17`, `strict pass=43/43`, '14/14 admitted', '43 entries' in files that should now say 48 / 15 / 18 / 44 - separate historical-by-design lines (append-only rule R6/R9: historical statements stay) from live-claim lines that now read wrong), SHONEN evidence pointers that no longer resolve, SCORECARD axis scores that contradict a cited counter. Output a table path:line -> statement -> observed value (command) -> classification stale-live|historical-ok. The L1 decides which get appended errata. Write {WD}/CritCalibration.md.""")

